<title>CANADA: Bombardier gets 6 more MOUs for CRJ-700.</title>
<headline>Bombardier gets 6 more MOUs for CRJ-700.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Inc said on Wednesday that Great China Airlines of Taiwan had signed a memorandum of understanding (MOU) for six Canadair Regional Jet Series 700 aircraft.</p>
<p>Making the impromptu announcement following a press conference, Pierre Lortie, president of Bombardier Regional Aircraft Division, said the MOU brings to 73 the total number of orders, options and MOUs for the new jet.</p>
<p>With the Great China Airlines agreement, Bombardier has four firm orders, 28 options and 41 MOUs for the CRJ-700, Lortie said.</p>
<p>((--Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
